@author "Claude (Anthropic)"

; toward .a keeps the side of .a where it is. An alignment is an incidence,
; so the side of .b folds over and lands .b on .a, which carries out
; (map .a onto .b) as well (ADR 0031).

paper square
fold (map .a onto .b) (toward .a)

; assert steps = 1
; assert .b = (0, 0)
